    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d10">

                <pb facs="0131" n="5" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg5"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A12/41: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bancroft</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-02-20T18:00:00+09:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 20,
                                1925—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 10 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>34. My 33, February 20, 4 p.m.<anchor n="13" xml:id="d10-f1"/> Have just seen
                    United Press cablegram that President Coolidge has received consent of England,
                    Japan and Italy and is waiting for consent of France before calling disarmament
                    conference.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bancroft</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
